ress><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>APPLIED MATERIALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI YOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An epitaxial growth device (1) comprises a process chamber (2) that includes a supply port (3) to supply reactive gas (Go) and an exhaust port (4) to discharge exhaust gas (Gh) from the chamber. The exhaust port (4) of the process chamber (2) is connected with an exhaust pipe (8) to deliver exhaust gas (Gh) to an exhaust processing device (7). The part exposed to exhaust gas (Gh) is covered with coating (C) including polyimide or Teflon to protect the interior of the exhaust pipe (8) from corrosion.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un appareil de croissance épitaxiale (1) qui comprend une chambre de traitement (2) dotée d'une entrée d'alimentation (3) en gaz réactif (Go), et d'une sortie d'évacuation (4) de gaz d'échappement (Gh) hors de la chambre. Cette sortie (4) de la chambre de traitement (2) est reliée à un tuyau d'échappement (8) qui fournit le gaz d'échappement (Gh) à un dispositif de traitement de gaz d'échappement (7). La partie exposée au gaz d'échappement (Gh) est recouverte d'un revêtement (C) à base de polyimide ou de Teflon, de manière à protéger l'intérieur du tuyau d'échappement (8) contre la corrosion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>